WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.401
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to

00:00:02.401 --> 00:00:03.870
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:06.805
Thank you for watching.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.805 --> 00:00:08.174
Thank you for being here.

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:10.776
Guys, it's a very busy time
in New York City,

00:00:10.776 --> 00:00:14.380
because the UN General Assembly
is officially under way.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:17.049
Yeah. More than
100 foreign leaders are in town

00:00:17.049 --> 00:00:19.119
to address the assembly,
while some are just here

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:21.821
to pick up a fiancé for 90 days.

00:00:23.589 --> 00:00:25.925
I love when the UN
General Assembly is in session.

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:27.226
There is no greater joy
than watching

00:00:27.226 --> 00:00:30.563
the president of Romania
walk into the M&amp;M store.

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:34.934
Seriously, when else
are you going to spot

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:37.636
the president of Latvia holding
one of those restaurant buzzers

00:00:37.636 --> 00:00:38.805
outside Bubba Gump Shrimp?

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:42.342
It's like, "Our table is ready.
Let's go."

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:43.576
Of course, the main focus of

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:46.579
this year's General Assembly
is fighting COVID.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:48.947
Yep, nothing like holding
a superspreader event

00:00:48.947 --> 00:00:51.017
to tackle a pandemic.

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:54.887 line:0%
There's actually some
real concern about

00:00:54.887 --> 00:00:56.322 line:0%
the General Assembly
turning into

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:59.025 line:0%
a superspreader event,
because -- and this is real --

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:03.596 line:0%
the UN is using the honor system
to check vaccinations.

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:06.198 line:0%
-Ooh!
-What? The honor system?

00:01:06.198 --> 00:01:07.500
I don't even trust
the honor system

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.102
when they give out candy
on Halloween.

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:10.303
It's like, "Please take one.

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:11.437
Oh, I know you're
going to take it.

00:01:11.437 --> 00:01:13.840
Honey, they took the bowl.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:16.275
We don't even
have a bowl anymore."

00:01:16.275 --> 00:01:17.510
Next, the UN
is going to be like,

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.545
"We believe further conflict
with the Taliban

00:01:19.545 --> 00:01:23.282
will be avoided thanks to our
latest pinkie promise."

00:01:23.282 --> 00:01:25.751 line:0%
The first leader
to speak this morning

00:01:25.751 --> 00:01:27.954 line:0%
and address the pandemic
was none other than

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:33.393 line:0%
the unvaccinated president of
Brazil, Jair Bolsonaro.

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:35.461 line:0%
Yeah, that's like attending
a weight-loss conference

00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:39.232 line:0%
and hearing, "Please welcome our
first speaker, Colonel Sanders."

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:42.902 line:0%
After Bolsonaro spoke,
President Biden

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:45.638 line:0%
then made his address
to the UN General Assembly.

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:47.473 line:0%
It was the first time he spoke
to a room of full of

00:01:47.473 --> 00:01:48.708 line:0%
world leaders
confidently knowing

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:51.010 line:0%
that they didn't have him
on mute.

00:01:54.146 --> 00:01:57.684
Yeah, Biden talked about
the pandemic, climate change,

00:01:57.684 --> 00:01:59.785
and the withdrawal from
Afghanistan.

00:01:59.785 --> 00:02:01.554
When he watched, former
president Trump was like,

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:04.357
"Pssh!
I got way more laughs than him.

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:06.493
Way more laughs."

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:08.862
People are talking about this.

00:02:08.862 --> 00:02:10.296
Today, the U.S. Space Force

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:13.465
unveiled a uniform prototype
for its members.

00:02:13.465 --> 00:02:14.600
Finally. Look at this.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.769
Hmm.

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:19.305
Right now, every New York City
doorman is like,

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:22.175
"Are we in the Space Force?

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:24.978
What?

00:02:24.978 --> 00:02:26.846
That's what we're wearing."

00:02:27.513 --> 00:02:28.981
Can we see it again?

00:02:28.981 --> 00:02:33.486
It looks like a line cook being
yelled at by Gordon Ramsay.

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:38.057
"Go to space with you, donkey!
Go to space!"

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:39.825
Seriously, by the time
you button up that jacket,

00:02:39.825 --> 00:02:42.829
the space war is going to be
over, you know?

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:45.231
Yep, that is the new uniform,
until Jeff Bezos

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:47.366
buys the Space Force
and turns it into this.

00:02:47.366 --> 00:02:51.437
Yeah, I love that.
He looks...

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:52.971
[ Applause ]

00:02:52.971 --> 00:02:55.441
He looks like a mash-up
of Buzz Lightyear and Woody,

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:57.142
doesn't he?

00:02:57.142 --> 00:02:58.444
Here's some good news.

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:01.380
Johnson &amp; Johnson announced
its COVID booster shot is

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:05.618
94% effective when given two
months after the first dose.

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:07.686
People who got
the J&amp;J were like,

00:03:07.686 --> 00:03:12.992
"Yeah, that would have been nice
to know about three months ago."

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.593
Actually, everyone
who got J&amp;J was like,

00:03:14.593 --> 00:03:15.628
"We already got boosters.

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:18.164
They're called Moderna. Yeah."

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:21.667
Well, this is great.

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:24.337
I saw that Google Meet --
Google Meet

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:27.506
is going to start automatically
adjusting webcam brightness

00:03:27.506 --> 00:03:29.074
in users's browsers.

00:03:29.074 --> 00:03:30.776
Yeah. And it's not the only
new feature they're adding.

00:03:30.776 --> 00:03:32.044
Take a look at this.

00:03:32.044 --> 00:03:33.879
-We here at Google Meet
are excited to announce

00:03:33.879 --> 00:03:38.050
a brand-new feature to make your
experience better than ever.

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:40.253
That's right --
when you click "New Meeting,"

00:03:40.253 --> 00:03:42.989
it will take you
directly to Zoom.

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:45.291
Google Meet --
at least we're not Skype.

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:48.261
-Yeah, isn't that amazing?
That's amazing.

00:03:52.965 --> 00:03:57.169 line:0%
And, finally, a pair of
107-year-old sisters in Japan

00:03:57.169 --> 00:04:00.673 line:0%
just claimed the title of
world's oldest identical twins.

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:02.175
Yeah, and just to
creep people out,

00:04:02.175 --> 00:04:04.276
they stand in the hallway of
their retirement home and say,

00:04:04.276 --> 00:04:06.145
"Come play with us."

00:04:06.145 --> 00:04:09.215
Guys, as I said before, this
week, the UN General Assembly,

00:04:09.215 --> 00:04:10.516
with leaders coming in
from all over the world,

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:11.951
is happening.

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:13.118
They're gonna give speeches.
They're gonna meet each other.

00:04:13.118 --> 00:04:14.887
But, sometimes, when
you meet new people,

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:16.656
it can be hard to break the ice,

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:18.123
which is why a lot
of leaders come prepared

00:04:18.123 --> 00:04:20.759
with their very own "getting
to know you" icebreakers.

00:04:20.759 --> 00:04:21.928
I'll show you what I mean.

00:04:21.928 --> 00:04:24.496
It's time for
"Tonight Show Icebreakers."

00:04:24.496 --> 00:04:30.169
-♪ "Tonight Show Icebreakers" ♪

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:34.540
-First up, we have British
Prime Minister Boris Johnson.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:38.678 line:0%
His icebreaker is, "Which fork
do you use to comb your hair?"

00:04:38.678 --> 00:04:40.613 line:0%
-Yeah.
-Yeah. It's a nice icebreaker.

00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:43.282 line:0%
-Yeah.
-Gets you into the conversation.

00:04:43.282 --> 00:04:46.852 line:0%
Next up, we have
Latvian President Egils Levits.

00:04:46.852 --> 00:04:48.788 line:0%
His icebreaker is...

00:04:51.557 --> 00:04:53.058 line:0%
-Good one.
-This is just icebreaking.

00:04:53.058 --> 00:04:54.626 line:0%
-Yeah, just break the ice.

00:04:54.626 --> 00:04:58.664 line:0%
-Next up is
Finnish President Niinisto.

00:04:58.664 --> 00:05:01.400 line:0%
His icebreaker is, "Sorry,
you might not recognize me

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:04.870 line:0%
without my Joker makeup."

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:06.105 line:0%
That's interesting.
It's an icebreaker.

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:07.306 line:0%
-Yeah.

00:05:07.306 --> 00:05:11.176 line:0%
-Here is Prime Minister
Bennett of Israel.

00:05:11.176 --> 00:05:14.780 line:0%
His icebreaker is, "Do you like
my resting kissy face?"

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:17.116 line:0%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:21.387 line:0%
-[ Smooching ]

00:05:21.387 --> 00:05:23.923 line:0%
-Up next, here is
U.S. President Joe Biden.

00:05:23.923 --> 00:05:25.858 line:0%
-Oh.
-His icebreaker is...

00:05:29.761 --> 00:05:32.398 line:0%
-That's his icebreaker?
-Wow.

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:33.933 line:0%
-Wow.

00:05:33.933 --> 00:05:37.202 line:0%
-Next is Estonian President
Kaljulaid.

00:05:37.202 --> 00:05:38.538 line:0%
Her icebreaker is...

00:05:41.573 --> 00:05:43.609 line:0%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:44.543 --> 00:05:47.646 line:0%
Next up, we have
Prime Minister Modi of India.

00:05:47.646 --> 00:05:50.115 line:0%
His icebreaker is, "Why does
Macy's keep offering me

00:05:50.115 --> 00:05:52.284 line:0%
a part-time job
for the holidays?"

00:05:52.284 --> 00:05:54.020 line:0%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:56.255 line:0%
-That's a good icebreaker.
-Yeah.

00:05:56.255 --> 00:06:00.859 line:0%
And, finally, here is Brazilian
President Jair Bolsonaro.

00:06:00.859 --> 00:06:03.462 line:0%
His icebreaker is,
"I'm unvaxxed, sashed,

00:06:03.462 --> 00:06:05.998 line:0%
and ready to get trashed."

00:06:05.998 --> 00:06:07.533 line:0%
That's all we have for
"Tonight Show Icebreakers."

